WEBVTT

00:00:02.678 --> 00:00:30.620
Oxford Bookworm Stage 1 One Way Ticket by Jennifer Bassett Published and copyright Oxford University Press 1992 The Girl with Green Eyes Of course, the man in the brown hat said There are good policemen, and there are bad policemen, you know."

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.262
You're right, the young man said.

00:00:34.322 --> 00:00:37.614
Yes, that's very true.

00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:39.634
Isn't it, Julie?

00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:43.146
He looked at the young woman next to him.

00:00:43.206 --> 00:00:46.718
Julie didn't answer and looked bored.

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:49.314
She closed her eyes.

00:00:49.374 --> 00:00:54.768
Julie's my wife, the young man told the man in the brown hat.

00:00:54.828 --> 00:00:56.920
She doesn't like trains.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:01.030
She always feels ill on trains.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:05.402
Oh yes, the man in the brown hat said.

00:01:05.462 --> 00:01:10.654
Now my wife, she doesn't like buses.

00:01:10.714 --> 00:01:14.446
She nearly had an accident on a bus once.

00:01:14.506 --> 00:01:16.476
It was last year.

00:01:16.536 --> 00:01:18.998
No, no it wasn't.

00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:20.820
It was two years ago.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.071
I remember now.

00:01:23.131 --> 00:01:25.602
It was in Manchester.

00:01:25.661 --> 00:01:32.693
He told a long, boring story about his wife and a bus in Manchester.

00:01:32.753 --> 00:01:37.274
It was a hot day and the train was slow.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:40.665
There were seven people in the carriage.

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:54.363
There was the man in the brown hat, the young man and his wife Julie, a mother and two children, and a tall, dark man in an expensive suit.

00:01:54.423 --> 00:01:57.684
The young man's name was Bill.

00:01:57.744 --> 00:02:02.116
He had short brown hair and a happy smile.

00:02:02.176 --> 00:02:08.177
His wife, Julie, had long red hair and very green eyes.

00:02:08.237 --> 00:02:10.568
The color of sea water.

00:02:10.628 --> 00:02:14.108
They were very beautiful eyes.

00:02:14.168 --> 00:02:18.882
The man in the brown hat talked and talked.

00:02:18.942 --> 00:02:22.746
He had a big red face and a loud voice.

00:02:22.806 --> 00:02:27.428
He talked to Bill because Bill liked to talk too.

00:02:27.488 --> 00:02:34.463
The man in the brown hat laughed a lot, and when he laughed, Bill laughed too.

00:02:34.523 --> 00:02:38.656
Bill liked talking and laughing with people.

00:02:38.716 --> 00:02:42.768
The two children were hot and bored.

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:45.414
They didn't want to sit down.

00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:50.740
They wanted to be noisy and run up and down the train.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.122
Now sit down and be quiet, their mother said.

00:02:56.182 --> 00:03:02.234
She was a small woman with a tired face and a tired voice.

00:03:02.294 --> 00:03:07.517
I don't want to sit down, the little boy said.

00:03:07.577 --> 00:03:10.165
I'm thirsty.

00:03:10.225 --> 00:03:15.284
Here, have an orange, his mother said.

00:03:15.344 --> 00:03:20.348
She took an orange out of her bag and gave it to him.

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:26.420
I want an orange too, the little girl said loudly.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.844
All right, here you are, said her mother.

00:03:30.904 --> 00:03:33.595
Eat it nicely now.

00:03:33.655 --> 00:03:39.673
The children ate their oranges and were quiet for a minute.

00:03:39.733 --> 00:03:44.900
Then the little boy said, I want a drink!

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.570
I'm thirsty!

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:54.154
The tall, dark man took out his newspaper and began to read.

00:03:54.213 --> 00:04:00.696
Julie opened her eyes and looked at the back page of his newspaper.

00:04:00.756 --> 00:04:07.171
She read about the weather in Budapest and about the football in Liverpool.

00:04:07.231 --> 00:04:18.038
She wasn't interested in Budapest, and she didn't like football, but she didn't want to listen to Bill and the man in the brown hat.

00:04:18.098 --> 00:04:22.121
Talk, talk, talk, she thought.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.732
Bill never stops talking.

00:04:25.792 --> 00:04:33.576
Then suddenly she saw the tall man's eyes over the top of his newspaper.

00:04:33.636 --> 00:04:39.916
She could not see his mouth but there was a smile in his eyes.

00:04:39.975 --> 00:04:47.768
Quickly, she looked down at the newspaper and read about the weather in Budapest again.

00:04:47.828 --> 00:04:54.382
The train stopped at Dourlish Station and people got on and got off.

00:04:54.442 --> 00:04:57.593
There was a lot of noise.

00:04:57.652 --> 00:05:00.694
Is this our station?

00:05:00.754 --> 00:05:02.865
The little girl asked.

00:05:02.925 --> 00:05:06.309
She went to the window and looked out.

00:05:06.369 --> 00:05:08.604
No, it isn't.

00:05:08.664 --> 00:05:12.687
Now sit down, her mother said.

00:05:12.747 --> 00:05:21.014
We're going to Penzance, the little girl told Bill, for our holidays.

00:05:21.074 --> 00:05:24.216
Yes, her mother said.

00:05:24.276 --> 00:05:28.250
My sisters got a little hotel by the sea.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.212
We're staying there.

00:05:30.272 --> 00:05:32.743
It's cheap, you see.

00:05:32.803 --> 00:05:38.845
Yes, the man in the brown hat said, it's a nice town.

00:05:38.865 --> 00:05:41.966
I know a man there.

00:05:42.026 --> 00:05:45.318
He's got a restaurant in King Street.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:48.599
A lot of holiday people go there.

00:05:48.659 --> 00:05:52.280
He makes a lot of money in the summer.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.622
He laughed loudly.

00:05:54.682 --> 00:06:01.708
Yes, he said again, you can have a nice holiday in Penzance.

00:06:01.768 --> 00:06:06.014
"'We're going to St. Ostal,' Bill said.

00:06:06.074 --> 00:06:07.666
Me and Julie.

00:06:07.726 --> 00:06:10.347
It's our first holiday.

00:06:10.406 --> 00:06:15.470
Julie wanted to go to Spain, but I like St. Ostal.

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:19.112
I always go there for my holidays.

00:06:19.172 --> 00:06:21.432
It's nice in August.

00:06:21.492 --> 00:06:24.884
You can have a good time there too.'

00:06:24.944 --> 00:06:27.596
Julie looked out of the window.

00:06:27.616 --> 00:06:31.278
"'Where is Buddha Pest?'

00:06:31.338 --> 00:06:32.729
she thought.

00:06:32.789 --> 00:06:35.412
I want to go there.

00:06:35.472 --> 00:06:42.808
I want to go to Vienna, to Paris, to Rome, to Athens.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:47.172
Her green eyes were bored and angry.

00:06:47.232 --> 00:06:53.156
Through the window she watched the little villages and hills of England.

00:06:53.216 --> 00:06:57.500
The man in the brown hat looked at Julie.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.899
You're right, he said to Bill.

00:07:00.959 --> 00:07:04.997
You can have a good time on holiday in England.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:09.119
We always go to Brighton, me and the wife.

00:07:09.179 --> 00:07:15.943
But the weather, we went one year and it rained every day.

00:07:16.003 --> 00:07:19.554
Morning, afternoon and night.

00:07:19.614 --> 00:07:20.996
It's true.

00:07:21.056 --> 00:07:24.047
It never stopped raining.

00:07:24.107 --> 00:07:26.318
He laughed loudly.

00:07:26.378 --> 00:07:30.017
We nearly went home after the first week.

00:07:30.077 --> 00:07:32.596
Bill laughed too.

00:07:32.655 --> 00:07:35.298
What did you do all day then?

00:07:35.358 --> 00:07:36.800
He asked.

00:07:36.859 --> 00:07:42.354
Julie read about the weather in Budapest for the third time.

00:07:42.414 --> 00:07:46.588
Then she looked at the tall man's hands.

00:07:46.648 --> 00:07:51.582
They were long, brown hands, very clean.

00:07:51.642 --> 00:07:55.064
Nice hands, she thought.

00:07:55.124 --> 00:07:59.289
He wore a very expensive Japanese watch.

00:07:59.349 --> 00:08:02.300
Japan," she thought.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.431
I'd like to go to Japan.

00:08:05.491 --> 00:08:11.843
She looked up and saw the man's eyes again over the top of his newspaper.

00:08:11.902 --> 00:08:15.623
This time she did not look away.

00:08:15.683 --> 00:08:24.466
Green eyes looked into dark brown eyes for a long, slow minute.

00:08:24.526 --> 00:08:32.411
After Newton Abbott's station, the guard came into the carriage to look at their tickets.

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:38.684
Now then, he said, where are we all going?

00:08:38.744 --> 00:08:45.027
This trains late, the man in the brown hat said.

00:08:45.088 --> 00:08:49.340
Twenty minutes late by my watch.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:54.736
Ten minutes, the guard said, that's all.

00:08:54.796 --> 00:08:57.718
He smiled at Julie.

00:08:57.778 --> 00:09:06.111
The tall, dark man put his newspaper down, found his ticket, and gave it to the guard.

00:09:06.171 --> 00:09:09.052
The guard looked at it.

00:09:09.112 --> 00:09:12.773
You're all right, sir, he said.

00:09:12.833 --> 00:09:16.994
The boat doesn't leave Plymouth before six o'clock.

00:09:17.054 --> 00:09:19.602
You've got lots of time.

00:09:19.662 --> 00:09:28.134
The tall man smiled, put his ticket back in his pocket, and opened his newspaper again.

00:09:28.194 --> 00:09:31.055
Julie didn't look at him.

00:09:31.116 --> 00:09:34.007
A boat, she thought.

00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:37.358
He's taking a boat from Plymouth.

00:09:37.418 --> 00:09:39.710
Where's he going?

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:44.808
She looked at him again with her long green eyes.

00:09:44.868 --> 00:09:49.214
He read his newspaper and didn't look at her.

00:09:49.274 --> 00:09:52.894
But his eyes smiled.

00:09:52.954 --> 00:10:00.216
The train stopped at Tottenham station and more people got on and off.

00:10:00.276 --> 00:10:04.887
Everybody's going on holiday, Bill said.

00:10:04.947 --> 00:10:06.647
He laughed.

00:10:06.707 --> 00:10:09.708
It's going to be wonderful.

00:10:09.768 --> 00:10:12.592
No work for two weeks.

00:10:12.652 --> 00:10:16.237
It's a nice, quiet town, St. Oster.

00:10:16.297 --> 00:10:24.522
We can stay in bed in the mornings, and sit and talk in the afternoons, and have a drink or two in the evenings.

00:10:24.582 --> 00:10:26.134
Hey, Julie.

00:10:26.194 --> 00:10:28.704
He looked at his wife.

00:10:28.764 --> 00:10:31.696
Are you all right, Julie?

00:10:31.757 --> 00:10:33.858
Yes, Bill.

00:10:33.918 --> 00:10:35.799
She said quietly.

00:10:35.859 --> 00:10:37.850
I'm okay.

00:10:37.911 --> 00:10:40.902
She looked out of the window again.

00:10:40.962 --> 00:10:45.926
The train went more quickly now, and it began to rain.

00:10:45.986 --> 00:10:51.510
Bill and the man in the brown hat talked and talked.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:11:00.147
Bill told a long story about two men and a dog, and the man in the brown hat laughed very loudly.

00:11:00.207 --> 00:11:04.260
That's a good story, he said.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.932
I like that.

00:11:05.992 --> 00:11:07.733
You tell it very well.

00:11:07.753 --> 00:11:17.154
Do you know the story about and he told Bill a story about a Frenchman and a bicycle.

00:11:17.214 --> 00:11:22.806
Why do people laugh at these stories, Julie thought?

00:11:22.866 --> 00:11:25.876
They're so boring!

00:11:25.936 --> 00:11:28.788
But Bill liked it.

00:11:28.848 --> 00:11:37.510
Then he told a story about an old woman and a cat, and the man in the brown hat laughed again.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.633
That's good, too!

00:11:40.693 --> 00:11:42.236
I don't know.

00:11:42.256 --> 00:11:45.707
How do you remember them all?

00:11:45.767 --> 00:11:51.640
Because, Julie thought, he tells them every day.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.651
I don't understand.

00:11:55.711 --> 00:11:58.162
The little girl said suddenly.

00:11:58.222 --> 00:12:00.743
She looked at Bill.

00:12:00.804 --> 00:12:03.364
Why did the cat die?

00:12:03.384 --> 00:12:05.876
Shhh.

00:12:05.936 --> 00:12:09.204
Be quiet, her mother said.

00:12:09.264 --> 00:12:12.452
Come and eat your sandwiches now.

00:12:12.512 --> 00:12:16.113
That's all right, Bill said.

00:12:16.174 --> 00:12:18.374
I like children.

00:12:18.434 --> 00:12:22.927
The man in the brown hat looked at the children's sandwiches.

00:12:22.947 --> 00:12:27.350
Mmm, I'm hungry too.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:33.804
He said, you can get sandwiches in the restaurant on this train.

00:12:33.864 --> 00:12:35.864
He looked at Bill.

00:12:35.924 --> 00:12:38.957
Let's go down to the restaurant, eh?

00:12:39.017 --> 00:12:41.728
I need a drink too."

00:12:41.788 --> 00:12:43.879
Bill laughed.

00:12:43.939 --> 00:12:45.569
You're right.

00:12:45.629 --> 00:12:49.330
It's thirsty work telling stories.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:53.781
The two men stood up and left the carriage.

00:12:53.841 --> 00:12:58.532
The little girl ate her sandwich and looked at Julie.

00:12:58.592 --> 00:13:01.763
But why did the cat die?

00:13:01.823 --> 00:13:03.353
She asked.

00:13:03.413 --> 00:13:06.474
I don't know, Julie said.

00:13:06.534 --> 00:13:09.472
Perhaps it wanted to die.

00:13:09.532 --> 00:13:12.980
The little girl came and sat next to Julie.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:16.541
"'I like your hair,' she said.

00:13:16.561 --> 00:13:19.562
"'It's beautiful!'

00:13:19.623 --> 00:13:23.734
Julie looked down at her and smiled.

00:13:23.794 --> 00:13:28.256
For some minutes it was quiet in the carriage.

00:13:28.316 --> 00:13:34.238
Then the tall, dark man opened his bag and took out a book.

00:13:34.298 --> 00:13:40.496
He put it on the seat next to him and looked at Julie with a smile.

00:13:40.555 --> 00:13:45.284
Julie looked back at him and then down at the book.

00:13:45.344 --> 00:13:49.248
Famous towns of Italy, she read.

00:13:49.308 --> 00:13:54.642
Venice, Florence, Rome, Naples.

00:13:54.702 --> 00:13:59.505
She looked away again, out of the window at the rain.

00:13:59.565 --> 00:14:07.701
Two weeks in St. Oster, she thought, with Bill, in the rain.

00:14:07.761 --> 00:14:13.491
After half an hour, The two men came back to the carriage.

00:14:13.551 --> 00:14:17.912
There are a lot of people on this train, Bill said.

00:14:17.972 --> 00:14:20.772
Do you want to sandwich, Julie?

00:14:20.832 --> 00:14:23.293
No, she said.

00:14:23.353 --> 00:14:25.054
I'm not hungry.

00:14:25.114 --> 00:14:27.264
You eat them.

00:14:27.324 --> 00:14:30.855
The train was nearly at Plymouth.

00:14:30.915 --> 00:14:35.166
Doors opened and people began to move.

00:14:35.226 --> 00:14:38.199
A lot of people get on here.

00:14:38.259 --> 00:14:48.578
The man in the brown hat said, The tall, dark man stood up and put his book and his newspaper in his bag.

00:14:48.638 --> 00:14:52.830
Then he picked up his bag and left the carriage.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:56.234
The train stopped at the station.

00:14:56.294 --> 00:15:03.488
A lot of people got on the train and two women and an old man came into the carriage.

00:15:03.548 --> 00:15:06.508
They had a lot of bags with them.

00:15:06.568 --> 00:15:12.407
Bill and the man in the brown hat stood up and helped them.

00:15:12.467 --> 00:15:16.698
One of the women had a big bag of apples.

00:15:16.758 --> 00:15:22.271
The bag broke and the apples went all over the carriage.

00:15:22.331 --> 00:15:24.642
Oh, damn!

00:15:24.702 --> 00:15:26.292
She said.

00:15:26.352 --> 00:15:31.474
Everybody laughed and helped her to find the apples.

00:15:31.534 --> 00:15:35.973
The train moved away from Plymouth Station.

00:15:36.033 --> 00:15:45.212
After a minute or two, everybody sat down, and the woman gave some apples to the children.

00:15:45.272 --> 00:15:47.922
Where's Julie?

00:15:47.982 --> 00:15:50.162
Bill said suddenly.

00:15:50.222 --> 00:15:52.573
She's not here.

00:15:52.633 --> 00:15:56.014
Perhaps she went to the restaurant.

00:15:56.074 --> 00:15:58.954
The man in the brown hat said.

00:15:59.014 --> 00:16:02.785
But she wasn't hungry, Bill said.

00:16:02.845 --> 00:16:05.019
She told me.

00:16:05.079 --> 00:16:08.875
The little girl looked at Bill.

00:16:08.935 --> 00:16:13.478
She got off the train at Plymouth, she said.

00:16:13.538 --> 00:16:17.472
With the tall, dark man, I saw them.

00:16:17.532 --> 00:16:21.214
Of course she didn't, Bill said.

00:16:21.274 --> 00:16:23.226
She's on this train.

00:16:23.286 --> 00:16:25.338
She didn't get off.

00:16:25.398 --> 00:16:27.398
Yes, she did.

00:16:27.458 --> 00:16:30.160
The children's mother said suddenly.

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:32.312
I saw her too.

00:16:32.372 --> 00:16:36.681
The tall man waited for her on the platform.

00:16:36.741 --> 00:16:40.038
He waited for her.

00:16:40.098 --> 00:16:42.660
Bill's mouth was open.

00:16:42.719 --> 00:16:47.682
But he read his newspaper all the time.

00:16:47.702 --> 00:16:52.784
He didn't talk to Julie, and she never talked to him.

00:16:52.804 --> 00:16:56.326
They didn't say a word.

00:16:56.386 --> 00:17:03.368
People don't always need words, young man, the children's mother said.

00:17:03.428 --> 00:17:06.415
But she's my wife!

00:17:06.475 --> 00:17:10.021
Bill's face was red and angry.

00:17:10.081 --> 00:17:12.512
She can't do that.

00:17:12.572 --> 00:17:14.392
He said loudly.

00:17:14.453 --> 00:17:16.233
He stood up.

00:17:16.293 --> 00:17:19.364
I'm going to stop the train.

00:17:19.425 --> 00:17:24.416
Everybody looked at him and the two children laughed.

00:17:24.476 --> 00:17:31.688
No, the man in the brown hat said, no, you don't want to do that.

00:17:31.748 --> 00:17:36.440
Sit down and eat your sandwiches, my friend.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:39.630
But I don't understand.

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:41.330
Why did she go?

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:45.021
What am I going to do?

00:17:45.082 --> 00:17:49.183
Bill's face was very unhappy.

00:17:49.243 --> 00:17:53.574
After a second or two, he sat down again.

00:17:53.634 --> 00:17:56.956
What am I going to do?

00:17:57.016 --> 00:17:59.326
He said again.

00:17:59.386 --> 00:18:01.547
Nothing.

00:18:01.607 --> 00:18:04.298
The man in the brown hat said.

00:18:04.358 --> 00:18:07.450
He ate his sandwich slowly.

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:11.632
Go and have your holiday in St. Austin.

00:18:11.692 --> 00:18:14.262
You can have a good time there.

00:18:14.322 --> 00:18:16.544
Forget about Julie.

00:18:16.604 --> 00:18:19.824
Those green eyes now.

00:18:19.884 --> 00:18:25.046
He took out a second sandwich and began to eat it.

00:18:25.106 --> 00:18:29.068
I knew a woman once with green eyes.

00:18:29.128 --> 00:18:32.860
She gave me a very bad time.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:34.541
No.

00:18:34.601 --> 00:18:43.000
You want to forget about Julie.

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:51.228
South for the winter.

00:18:51.288 --> 00:18:56.570
I never stay in one country for a long time.

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.981
It gets boring.

00:18:59.042 --> 00:19:05.644
I like to move on, see new places, meet different people.

00:19:05.704 --> 00:19:09.815
It's a good life most of the time.

00:19:09.875 --> 00:19:14.216
When I need money, I get a job.

00:19:14.276 --> 00:19:23.150
I can do most things hotel and restaurant work, building work, picking fruit.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:28.122
In Europe, you can pick fruit most of the year.

00:19:28.183 --> 00:19:33.506
You need to be in the right country at the right time, of course.

00:19:33.566 --> 00:19:38.919
It's not easy work, but the money's not bad.

00:19:38.979 --> 00:19:43.072
I like to go south in the winter.

00:19:43.132 --> 00:19:46.100
Life is easier in the sun.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:50.981
and Northern Europe can get very cold in the winter.

00:19:51.041 --> 00:19:55.824
Last year, 1989 it was.

00:19:55.884 --> 00:19:59.166
I was in Venice for October.

00:19:59.226 --> 00:20:03.570
I did some work in a hotel for three weeks.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:07.752
Then I began slowly to move south.

00:20:07.812 --> 00:20:11.774
I always go by train when I can.

00:20:11.834 --> 00:20:14.262
I like trains.

00:20:14.322 --> 00:20:20.650
You can walk about on a train and you meet a lot of people.

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:25.391
I left Venice and went on to Trieste.

00:20:25.451 --> 00:20:33.504
There, I got a cheap ticket for the slow train to Sofia in Bulgaria.

00:20:33.564 --> 00:20:42.057
This train goes all down through Yugoslavia and takes a long time, a day and a half.

00:20:42.117 --> 00:20:45.176
But that didn't matter to me.

00:20:45.236 --> 00:20:51.425
The train left Trieste at nine o'clock on a Thursday morning.

00:20:51.485 --> 00:20:58.436
There weren't many people on it at first, but at Zagreb, more people got on.

00:20:58.496 --> 00:21:04.038
Two girls went along the corridor, past my carriage.

00:21:04.098 --> 00:21:08.929
They looked through the door, but they didn't come in.

00:21:08.989 --> 00:21:15.353
Then an old woman came in, sat down, and went to sleep.

00:21:15.413 --> 00:21:22.548
The two girls came back along the corridor and looked into the carriage again.

00:21:22.608 --> 00:21:29.471
The train left Zagreb, and I looked out of the window for about ten minutes.

00:21:29.531 --> 00:21:32.742
Then I went to sleep too.

00:21:32.802 --> 00:21:39.294
When I opened my eyes again, the two girls were in the carriage.

00:21:39.355 --> 00:21:43.536
They looked friendly, so I said, hello?

00:21:43.596 --> 00:21:46.256
Hi, they said.

00:21:46.316 --> 00:21:49.056
You're American, I said.

00:21:49.116 --> 00:21:51.656
Or Canadian, right?

00:21:51.716 --> 00:21:55.378
American, the taller girl said.

00:21:55.438 --> 00:21:57.188
She smiled.

00:21:57.248 --> 00:22:00.150
And you're 23.

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:03.231
Your name's Tom Walsh.

00:22:03.291 --> 00:22:05.842
You've got blue eyes.

00:22:05.902 --> 00:22:09.663
And your mom lives in Burnham on C.

00:22:09.723 --> 00:22:11.744
U.K., right?

00:22:11.804 --> 00:22:15.345
How did you know all that, I asked?

00:22:15.405 --> 00:22:18.106
The second girl laughed.

00:22:18.166 --> 00:22:21.116
She looked at your passport.

00:22:21.176 --> 00:22:23.616
It's in your coat pocket.

00:22:23.676 --> 00:22:25.827
Oh, right.

00:22:25.887 --> 00:22:29.818
My coat was on the seat next to me.

00:22:29.878 --> 00:22:36.309
I took my passport out of my pocket and put it back in my bag.

00:22:36.369 --> 00:22:38.269
Who are you then?

00:22:38.329 --> 00:22:39.590
I asked.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:41.611
They told me.

00:22:41.671 --> 00:22:47.114
Melanie and Carol from Los Angeles, USA.

00:22:47.174 --> 00:22:50.106
They liked Europe, they said.

00:22:50.166 --> 00:23:07.084
They knew a lot of places, Britain, Holland, Denmark, Germany, France, Spain, Italy, Yugoslavia, Bulgaria, Greece.

00:23:07.144 --> 00:23:10.818
I'm going to Bulgaria now, I said.

00:23:10.878 --> 00:23:12.872
for about a month.

00:23:12.932 --> 00:23:19.654
Then I'm going south for the winter, Cyprus, or perhaps North Africa.

00:23:19.714 --> 00:23:22.154
Oh yes, they said.

00:23:22.214 --> 00:23:24.595
We love Bulgaria.

00:23:24.655 --> 00:23:26.845
Sophia's a great town.

00:23:26.905 --> 00:23:28.395
Wonderful.

00:23:28.456 --> 00:23:31.146
What do you do about money?

00:23:31.206 --> 00:23:32.336
I asked.

00:23:32.396 --> 00:23:36.467
Well, you know, Carol smiled.

00:23:36.527 --> 00:23:40.014
Sometimes we get a little job.

00:23:40.074 --> 00:23:41.750
This and that.

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:43.270
But what about you?"

00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:47.511
"'Yeah, come on,' Melanie said.

00:23:47.531 --> 00:23:55.394
"'Tell us about you,' Tom Walsh, with the blue eyes, and the mum and burner man see.

00:23:55.414 --> 00:23:58.534
"'What are you doing with your life, hey?'

00:23:58.554 --> 00:24:01.466
"'So I told them.

00:24:01.526 --> 00:24:03.586
They were nice girls.

00:24:03.646 --> 00:24:09.310
They were older than me, perhaps 27 or 28, but I liked them.

00:24:09.370 --> 00:24:13.884
We talked and laughed for hours.

00:24:13.944 --> 00:24:18.276
I told them a lot of stories about my life.

00:24:18.336 --> 00:24:22.467
Some of the stories were true, some weren't.

00:24:22.527 --> 00:24:27.198
But the girls laughed and said I was a great guy.

00:24:27.258 --> 00:24:32.510
I asked them about Bulgaria because I didn't know the country.

00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:36.161
They knew Sophia well, they said.

00:24:36.221 --> 00:24:38.152
Hey, Carol.

00:24:38.212 --> 00:24:39.594
Melanie said.

00:24:39.654 --> 00:24:44.280
We're staying in Bela Palanca for a day or two.

00:24:44.340 --> 00:24:49.964
But let's go over to Sophia this weekend and meet Tom there.

00:24:50.024 --> 00:24:55.627
We can meet him on Saturday night at the hotel Marmara.

00:24:55.687 --> 00:25:00.550
Yeah, it's a good hotel, Carol told me.

00:25:00.610 --> 00:25:02.721
Cheap but good.

00:25:02.782 --> 00:25:05.013
What do you think, Tom?

00:25:05.073 --> 00:25:06.834
Great, I said.

00:25:06.894 --> 00:25:08.774
Let's do that.

00:25:08.834 --> 00:25:12.433
The train was very slow.

00:25:12.494 --> 00:25:19.468
We got to Belgrade at six o'clock in the evening, and a lot of people got off.

00:25:19.529 --> 00:25:24.182
They were only me and the girls in the carriage then.

00:25:24.242 --> 00:25:29.795
The guard came and looked at our tickets, and went away again.

00:25:29.855 --> 00:25:33.067
Carol looked at Melanie.

00:25:33.128 --> 00:25:36.540
Hey, Mel, she said.

00:25:36.600 --> 00:25:41.664
Why don't you and Tom go along to the restaurant?

00:25:41.724 --> 00:25:46.658
I'm not hungry, and I want to sleep for an hour.

00:25:46.718 --> 00:25:51.960
Food's very expensive on the train, I said.

00:25:52.020 --> 00:25:55.092
I haven't got much money just now.

00:25:55.153 --> 00:25:58.424
I'm going to get a job in Sofia.

00:25:58.484 --> 00:26:04.180
Oh, Tom, Melanie said, why didn't you tell us?

00:26:04.240 --> 00:26:08.023
Look, you're a nice guy, right?

00:26:08.083 --> 00:26:10.834
We're okay for money this week.

00:26:10.894 --> 00:26:13.165
We can buy you a meal.

00:26:13.225 --> 00:26:16.786
Of course we can, Terrell said.

00:26:16.846 --> 00:26:23.229
And look, in Sofia, we can take you to the best restaurant in town.

00:26:23.289 --> 00:26:26.430
It's a great place, we love it.

00:26:26.490 --> 00:26:28.080
What could I say?

00:26:28.100 --> 00:26:33.211
I was hungry, they had money, I didn't.

00:26:33.271 --> 00:26:38.392
so Melanie and I went to the restaurant and had a meal.

00:26:38.452 --> 00:26:43.914
When we came back, Carol was still alone in the carriage.

00:26:43.974 --> 00:26:48.516
Melanie put her feet on the seat and went to sleep.

00:26:48.576 --> 00:26:56.680
At Niss, some more people got on the train and two old men came into our carriage.

00:26:56.740 --> 00:27:02.528
They looked at Melanie's feet on the seat and talked in loud voices.

00:27:02.588 --> 00:27:08.507
Carol laughed, and Melanie opened her eyes and set up.

00:27:08.567 --> 00:27:11.510
Are we nearly there?

00:27:11.570 --> 00:27:15.132
She asked Carol and looked out of the window.

00:27:15.192 --> 00:27:19.475
Yeah, about half an hour, I think.

00:27:19.535 --> 00:27:23.208
Why are you getting off at Bela Palanca?

00:27:23.268 --> 00:27:24.288
I asked.

00:27:24.348 --> 00:27:26.870
What are you going to do there?

00:27:26.931 --> 00:27:29.142
Melanie smiled.

00:27:29.202 --> 00:27:36.184
Find a cheap hotel, meet people, Take a look at the town, you know.

00:27:36.244 --> 00:27:39.735
Just for a day or two, Carol said.

00:27:39.795 --> 00:27:42.156
But there's nothing there.

00:27:42.216 --> 00:27:46.888
Oh, well, you never know, Melanie Loft.

00:27:46.948 --> 00:27:49.498
See you in Sofia, right?

00:27:49.558 --> 00:27:51.719
On Saturday night.

00:27:51.779 --> 00:27:55.540
The hotel, Marmara, OK?

00:27:55.600 --> 00:27:58.122
8 o'clock, Carol said.

00:27:58.182 --> 00:28:00.122
Don't forget now.

00:28:00.182 --> 00:28:03.022
OK, great, I said.

00:28:03.082 --> 00:28:04.993
See you there.

00:28:05.053 --> 00:28:09.556
The train came into Bela Palanca and stopped.

00:28:09.616 --> 00:28:13.748
The two girls got off and stood on the platform.

00:28:13.808 --> 00:28:16.720
They smiled at me through the window.

00:28:16.780 --> 00:28:21.302
Saturday, eight o'clock, Melanie shouted.

00:28:21.362 --> 00:28:23.843
Okay, I called.

00:28:23.903 --> 00:28:28.316
They couldn't hear me because of the noise in the station.

00:28:28.376 --> 00:28:33.662
They smiled again, picked up their bags and walked away.

00:28:33.722 --> 00:28:35.678
Nice girls.

00:28:35.738 --> 00:28:42.140
I'm going to have a great time in Sofia, I thought.

00:28:42.200 --> 00:28:50.314
The train left Yugoslavia and crossed into Bulgaria at two o'clock in the morning.

00:28:50.374 --> 00:28:53.435
Then the train stopped at some village.

00:28:53.495 --> 00:28:55.826
I don't remember the name.

00:28:55.886 --> 00:28:59.658
I ate an apple and looked out of the window.

00:28:59.718 --> 00:29:04.644
Suddenly, there were a lot of policemen on the train.

00:29:04.704 --> 00:29:09.302
Everybody in the carriage sat up and began to talk.

00:29:09.362 --> 00:29:11.403
What's happening?

00:29:11.463 --> 00:29:15.155
I said in Italian to the old man next to me.

00:29:15.215 --> 00:29:17.246
I don't know.

00:29:17.306 --> 00:29:19.547
He said in bad Italian.

00:29:19.607 --> 00:29:22.659
Perhaps they're looking for somebody.

00:29:22.719 --> 00:29:24.039
Look!

00:29:24.100 --> 00:29:28.962
The police are taking some people off the train.

00:29:29.022 --> 00:29:33.174
Then two policemen came into our carriage.

00:29:33.234 --> 00:29:35.160
A tall thin one.

00:29:35.221 --> 00:29:37.506
and a short fat one.

00:29:37.567 --> 00:29:41.067
They looked at everybody carefully.

00:29:41.128 --> 00:29:44.679
And then they looked at me again.

00:29:44.739 --> 00:29:47.530
Come with us, please.

00:29:47.590 --> 00:29:50.600
The fat policeman said in English.

00:29:50.660 --> 00:29:52.301
What?

00:29:52.321 --> 00:29:52.611
Me?

00:29:52.671 --> 00:29:53.682
I said.

00:29:53.742 --> 00:29:54.842
Why?

00:29:54.902 --> 00:29:56.442
What's the matter?

00:29:56.502 --> 00:29:59.664
And bring your bag with you.

00:29:59.724 --> 00:30:02.514
The tall policeman said.

00:30:02.574 --> 00:30:10.938
I began to ask a question, but policemen never liked questions from young men with long hair.

00:30:10.998 --> 00:30:17.512
So I stayed quiet, picked up my bag and went with them.

00:30:17.572 --> 00:30:25.238
In the station building, there were a lot more policemen and some people from the train.

00:30:25.298 --> 00:30:29.010
They were all young people I saw.

00:30:29.070 --> 00:30:40.402
Some were afraid, some were bored, The police looked in everybody's bags and then the people went back to the train.

00:30:40.462 --> 00:30:44.534
My two policemen took me to a table.

00:30:44.594 --> 00:30:47.196
Your passport, please.

00:30:47.256 --> 00:30:51.938
The fat policeman said, and opened your bag.

00:30:51.999 --> 00:30:57.452
They looked at my passport and I opened my bag.

00:30:57.512 --> 00:31:02.914
There was a young police woman with red hair at the next table.

00:31:02.974 --> 00:31:09.266
she had a nice face, so I smiled at her and she smiled back.

00:31:09.326 --> 00:31:11.056
Aha!

00:31:11.116 --> 00:31:14.357
The tall policeman said suddenly.

00:31:14.418 --> 00:31:19.660
All my dirty shirts and clothes were out on the table.

00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:24.822
The policeman picked up my bag and turned it over.

00:31:24.882 --> 00:31:35.162
On to the table, out of my bag, fell packet after packet of US American dollars.

00:31:35.222 --> 00:31:38.446
Nice new dollars.

00:31:38.506 --> 00:31:42.188
Fifty dollar notes in big packets.

00:31:42.248 --> 00:31:44.940
A lot of money.

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:49.414
My mouth opened and stayed open.

00:31:49.474 --> 00:31:52.366
I couldn't find my voice.

00:31:52.426 --> 00:31:57.125
I was suddenly a very interesting person.

00:31:57.184 --> 00:32:03.054
and a lot of police ran up to our table and stood behind me.

00:32:03.114 --> 00:32:17.286
Fifty thousand, a hundred thousand, a hundred and fifty thousand, there's two hundred thousand dollars here, the tall policeman said.

00:32:17.346 --> 00:32:23.350
What an interesting bag, Mr. Tom Warsh!

00:32:23.410 --> 00:32:26.792
I found my voice again quickly.

00:32:26.852 --> 00:32:30.964
But it's not my bag, I shouted.

00:32:31.024 --> 00:32:36.569
There was a big, happy smile on that policeman's face.

00:32:36.629 --> 00:32:42.894
Well, he said, it's got your name on it, look.

00:32:42.954 --> 00:32:45.146
So I looked.

00:32:45.206 --> 00:32:48.429
And of course, there was my name.

00:32:48.489 --> 00:32:52.372
And yes, of course, it was my bag.

00:32:52.432 --> 00:32:56.273
So how did two hundred thousand U.S.

00:32:56.333 --> 00:32:59.134
dollars get into my bag?

00:32:59.194 --> 00:33:01.905
You cannot bring a U.S.

00:33:01.965 --> 00:33:06.476
dollars into this country, the fat policeman said.

00:33:06.536 --> 00:33:11.667
He had very short gray hair and little black eyes.

00:33:11.727 --> 00:33:14.358
He didn't smile once.

00:33:14.418 --> 00:33:18.949
But I didn't bring them, I said quickly.

00:33:19.009 --> 00:33:21.506
They're not my dollars.

00:33:21.566 --> 00:33:29.308
I never saw them before in my life, and there was a lot of noise in the station.

00:33:29.368 --> 00:33:33.622
I looked out of the window and saw my train.

00:33:33.682 --> 00:33:37.004
Slowly it began to move.

00:33:37.064 --> 00:33:38.125
Hey!

00:33:38.186 --> 00:33:39.086
I shouted.

00:33:39.146 --> 00:33:41.158
That's my train!"

00:33:41.218 --> 00:33:44.290
The tall policeman laughed.

00:33:44.350 --> 00:33:48.422
It was a great day for him.

00:33:48.482 --> 00:33:53.484
You're not getting back on that train.

00:33:53.544 --> 00:34:00.319
You're staying here with us in our beautiful country."

00:34:00.380 --> 00:34:03.192
He smiled happily.

00:34:03.252 --> 00:34:08.434
So I never got to Sophia on Saturday.

00:34:08.495 --> 00:34:11.717
I was very unhappy about that.

00:34:11.778 --> 00:34:16.640
I wanted to have a little talk with Melanie and Carol.

00:34:16.700 --> 00:34:20.463
Ask them one or two questions, you know.

00:34:20.523 --> 00:34:23.354
You're a nice guy, Tom.

00:34:23.414 --> 00:34:26.206
See you in Sofia, OK?

00:34:26.266 --> 00:34:29.687
Take you to the best restaurant in town.

00:34:29.747 --> 00:34:32.328
Yeah, great.

00:34:32.388 --> 00:34:38.262
And I never got down to Cyprus or North Africa that winter.

00:34:38.322 --> 00:34:42.013
Oh, well, I live and learn.

00:34:42.073 --> 00:34:45.675
It's not an easy life in prison.

00:34:45.735 --> 00:34:48.386
But it's warm in winter.

00:34:48.446 --> 00:34:50.855
And the food's not bad.

00:34:50.915 --> 00:34:54.704
And I'm meeting some interesting people.

00:34:54.764 --> 00:34:59.105
There's a man from Georgia, USSR.

00:34:59.165 --> 00:35:01.286
Boris, his name is.

00:35:01.346 --> 00:35:04.736
He comes from a place by the Black Sea.

00:35:04.796 --> 00:35:07.047
He's a great guy.

00:35:07.107 --> 00:35:12.468
When we get out of here, he and I are going down to Australia.

00:35:12.528 --> 00:35:15.659
Brisbane, perhaps, or Sydney.

00:35:15.719 --> 00:35:18.050
Get a job on a ship.

00:35:18.110 --> 00:35:20.371
Start a new life.

00:35:20.431 --> 00:35:30.704
Yeah, next year's going to be okay.

00:35:30.764 --> 00:35:39.566
Mr. Harris under night train.

00:35:39.626 --> 00:35:43.206
Mr. Harris liked trains.

00:35:43.266 --> 00:35:46.878
He was afraid of aeroplanes and didn't like buses.

00:35:46.938 --> 00:35:52.042
but trains, they were big and noisy and exciting.

00:35:52.102 --> 00:35:55.662
When he was a boy of ten, he liked trains.

00:35:55.722 --> 00:36:00.254
Now he was a man of fifty, and he still liked trains.

00:36:00.314 --> 00:36:05.225
So he was a happy man on the night of the 14th of September.

00:36:05.285 --> 00:36:13.107
He was on the night train from Helsinki to Ulou in Finland, and he had ten hours in front of him.

00:36:13.167 --> 00:36:16.590
I've got a book and my newspaper.

00:36:16.650 --> 00:36:25.964
He thought, and there's a good restaurant on the train, and then I've got two weeks holiday with my Finnish friends in Ulu.

00:36:26.024 --> 00:36:32.485
There weren't many people on the train, and nobody came into Mr. Harris's carriage.

00:36:32.545 --> 00:36:34.716
He was happy about that.

00:36:34.776 --> 00:36:43.328
Most people on the train slept through the night, but Mr. Harris liked to look out of the window and to read and think.

00:36:43.388 --> 00:36:52.317
After dinner in the restaurant, Mr. Harris came back to his carriage and sat in his seat next to the window.

00:36:52.377 --> 00:36:58.199
For an hour or two he watched the trees and lakes of Finland out of the window.

00:36:58.260 --> 00:37:04.282
Then it began to get dark, so he opened his book and began to read.

00:37:04.342 --> 00:37:09.623
At midnight the train stopped at the small station of Otova.

00:37:09.684 --> 00:37:14.438
Mr. Harris looked out of the window, but he saw nobody.

00:37:14.498 --> 00:37:19.712
The train moved away from the station into the black night again.

00:37:19.772 --> 00:37:25.583
Then the door of Mr. Harris's carriage opened and two people came in.

00:37:25.644 --> 00:37:28.414
A young man and a young woman.

00:37:28.475 --> 00:37:31.026
The young woman was angry.

00:37:31.086 --> 00:37:38.108
She closed the door and shouted at the man, Carl, you can't do this to me.

00:37:38.168 --> 00:37:42.572
The young man laughed loudly and sat down.

00:37:42.632 --> 00:37:46.867
Mr. Harris was a small, quiet man.

00:37:46.927 --> 00:37:50.988
He wore quiet clothes, and he had a quiet voice.

00:37:51.048 --> 00:37:57.230
He did not like noisy people and loud voices, so he was not pleased.

00:37:57.290 --> 00:38:01.621
Young people are always noisy, he thought.

00:38:01.681 --> 00:38:05.032
Why can't they talk quietly?

00:38:05.092 --> 00:38:08.902
He put his book down and closed his eyes.

00:38:08.962 --> 00:38:10.802
But he could not sleep.

00:38:10.862 --> 00:38:14.454
because the two young people didn't stop talking.

00:38:14.514 --> 00:38:23.350
The young woman sat down and said in a quieter voice, Carl, you're my brother, and I love you.

00:38:23.410 --> 00:38:25.650
But please listen to me.

00:38:25.710 --> 00:38:28.752
You can't take my diamond necklace.

00:38:28.812 --> 00:38:32.024
Give it back to me now, please.

00:38:32.084 --> 00:38:34.236
Carl smiled.

00:38:34.296 --> 00:38:39.806
No, Elena, he said, I'm going back to Russia soon.

00:38:39.866 --> 00:38:43.186
and I'm taking your diamonds with me.

00:38:43.246 --> 00:38:46.898
He took off his hat and put it on the seat.

00:38:46.958 --> 00:38:48.880
Elena, listen.

00:38:48.940 --> 00:38:53.964
You have a rich husband, but I, I have no money.

00:38:53.984 --> 00:38:55.926
I have nothing.

00:38:55.986 --> 00:38:58.648
How can I live without money?

00:38:58.708 --> 00:39:03.891
You can't give me money, so I need your diamonds, little sister."

00:39:03.952 --> 00:39:07.156
Mr. Harris looked at the young woman.

00:39:07.216 --> 00:39:10.938
She was small with black hair and dark eyes.

00:39:10.998 --> 00:39:13.889
Her face was white and afraid.

00:39:13.949 --> 00:39:17.720
Mr. Harris began to feel sorry for Elena.

00:39:17.780 --> 00:39:21.111
She and her brother didn't look at him once.

00:39:21.171 --> 00:39:22.961
Can't they see me?

00:39:22.981 --> 00:39:24.752
He thought.

00:39:24.812 --> 00:39:26.472
Car?

00:39:26.532 --> 00:39:27.992
Elena said.

00:39:28.053 --> 00:39:33.534
Her voice was very quiet now, and Mr. Harris listened carefully.

00:39:33.594 --> 00:39:40.974
You came to dinner at our house tonight and you went to my room and took my diamond necklace.

00:39:41.034 --> 00:39:43.605
How could you do that to me?

00:39:43.666 --> 00:39:46.647
My husband gave the diamonds to me.

00:39:46.708 --> 00:39:49.870
They were his mother's diamonds before that.

00:39:49.930 --> 00:39:55.022
He's going to be very, very angry, and I'm afraid of him."

00:39:55.082 --> 00:39:57.044
Her brother laughed.

00:39:57.104 --> 00:40:03.118
He put his hand in his pocket, then took it out again, and opened it slowly.

00:40:03.178 --> 00:40:07.030
The diamond necklace in his hand was very beautiful.

00:40:07.090 --> 00:40:09.720
Mr. Harris stared at it.

00:40:09.781 --> 00:40:14.954
For a minute or two nobody moved, and it was quiet in the carriage.

00:40:15.014 --> 00:40:21.668
There was only the noise of the train, and it went quickly on through the dark, cold night.

00:40:21.728 --> 00:40:26.280
Mr. Harris opened his book again, but he didn't read it.

00:40:26.340 --> 00:40:31.874
He watched Carl's face with its hungry eyes and its cold smile.

00:40:31.934 --> 00:40:36.911
What beautiful, beautiful diamonds, Carl said.

00:40:36.972 --> 00:40:39.738
I can get a lot of money for these.

00:40:39.798 --> 00:40:42.370
Give them back to me, Carl."

00:40:42.430 --> 00:40:43.900
Elena whispered.

00:40:43.960 --> 00:40:46.522
My husband's going to kill me.

00:40:46.582 --> 00:40:48.253
You're my brother.

00:40:48.313 --> 00:40:49.964
Please help me.

00:40:50.024 --> 00:40:51.434
Please.

00:40:51.495 --> 00:40:53.246
Carl laughed again.

00:40:53.266 --> 00:40:56.208
And Mr. Harris wanted to hit him.

00:40:56.268 --> 00:40:58.949
Go home, little sister.

00:40:59.009 --> 00:41:03.241
Carl said, I'm not going to give the diamonds back to you.

00:41:03.301 --> 00:41:06.560
Go home to your angry husband.

00:41:06.620 --> 00:41:13.029
Suddenly there was a knife in the young woman's hand, a long, bright knife.

00:41:13.089 --> 00:41:16.230
Mr. Harris watched with his mouth open.

00:41:16.290 --> 00:41:18.720
He couldn't speak or move.

00:41:18.781 --> 00:41:21.122
Give the diamonds back to me!

00:41:21.182 --> 00:41:22.602
Elena cried.

00:41:22.662 --> 00:41:24.592
Or I'm going to kill you!

00:41:24.652 --> 00:41:27.514
Her hand on the knife was white.

00:41:27.574 --> 00:41:30.034
Car laughed and laughed.

00:41:30.094 --> 00:41:31.805
What a sister!

00:41:31.865 --> 00:41:32.795
He said!

00:41:32.855 --> 00:41:36.248
What a kind, sweet sister!

00:41:36.308 --> 00:41:37.350
No!

00:41:37.410 --> 00:41:39.842
They're my diamonds now!

00:41:39.902 --> 00:41:43.436
Put your knife away, little sister!"

00:41:43.496 --> 00:41:48.388
But the knife in the white hand moved quickly, up, then down.

00:41:48.448 --> 00:41:54.743
There was a long, terrible cry, and Carl's body fell slowly onto the seat.

00:41:54.804 --> 00:42:02.950
The colour of the seat began to change to red, and the diamond necklace fell from Carl's hand onto the floor.

00:42:03.010 --> 00:42:05.713
Elena's face was white.

00:42:05.773 --> 00:42:07.096
Oh, no!

00:42:07.156 --> 00:42:08.296
she whispered.

00:42:08.356 --> 00:42:09.577
Carl!

00:42:09.637 --> 00:42:11.078
Come back!

00:42:11.138 --> 00:42:12.819
Come back!

00:42:12.879 --> 00:42:15.310
I didn't want to kill you!

00:42:15.370 --> 00:42:21.304
But Carl didn't answer, and the red blood ran slowly over the floor.

00:42:21.364 --> 00:42:27.798
Elena put her head in her hands, and again in the carriage there was a long, terrible cry.

00:42:27.858 --> 00:42:30.890
Mr. Harris's face was white, too.

00:42:30.950 --> 00:42:34.232
He opened his mouth, but he couldn't speak.

00:42:34.292 --> 00:42:38.033
He stood up and carefully moved to the door.

00:42:38.093 --> 00:42:40.754
The young woman was quiet now.

00:42:40.814 --> 00:42:44.434
She didn't move or look up at Mr. Harris.

00:42:44.495 --> 00:42:47.565
In the corridor, Mr. Harris ran.

00:42:47.626 --> 00:42:53.247
The guard was at the back of the train and Mr. Harris got there in half a minute.

00:42:53.307 --> 00:42:57.308
Quickly, Mr. Harris said, come quickly!

00:42:57.368 --> 00:42:58.798
An accident!

00:42:58.859 --> 00:43:00.309
A young woman!

00:43:00.369 --> 00:43:01.619
Oh dear!

00:43:01.679 --> 00:43:03.170
Her brother is...

00:43:03.230 --> 00:43:05.025
his dead!

00:43:05.085 --> 00:43:09.100
The guard ran with Mr. Harris back to the carriage.

00:43:09.160 --> 00:43:12.971
Mr. Harris opened the door, and they went inside.

00:43:13.031 --> 00:43:16.612
There was no dead body of a young man.

00:43:16.672 --> 00:43:18.682
There was no young woman.

00:43:18.742 --> 00:43:20.122
No blood.

00:43:20.182 --> 00:43:21.413
No knife.

00:43:21.473 --> 00:43:23.643
No diamond necklace.

00:43:23.703 --> 00:43:27.644
Only Mr. Harris's bags and his hat and coat.

00:43:27.704 --> 00:43:32.854
The guard looked at Mr. Harris, and Mr. Harris looked at him.

00:43:32.915 --> 00:43:35.907
But, Mr. Harris began.

00:43:35.967 --> 00:43:38.040
But they were here.

00:43:38.100 --> 00:43:39.731
I saw them.

00:43:39.791 --> 00:43:43.893
She, the young woman, she had a knife.

00:43:43.954 --> 00:43:47.326
And she, she killed her brother.

00:43:47.386 --> 00:43:49.887
A knife, you say?

00:43:49.947 --> 00:43:51.198
The guard asked.

00:43:51.258 --> 00:43:53.990
Yes, Mr. Harris said quickly.

00:43:54.050 --> 00:43:55.490
A long knife.

00:43:55.550 --> 00:43:57.752
And her brother took her diamonds.

00:43:57.812 --> 00:44:01.674
So she, ah, diamonds.

00:44:01.734 --> 00:44:03.291
The guard said.

00:44:03.351 --> 00:44:06.650
was the young woman's name, Elena?"

00:44:06.710 --> 00:44:07.930
he asked.

00:44:07.990 --> 00:44:11.443
Yes, it was, Mr. Harris said.

00:44:11.503 --> 00:44:13.434
How do you know that?

00:44:13.495 --> 00:44:14.846
Do you?

00:44:14.906 --> 00:44:16.958
Do you know her?

00:44:17.018 --> 00:44:23.112
Yes, and no, the guard said slowly.

00:44:23.172 --> 00:44:27.736
He thought for a minute, then looked at Mr. Harris.

00:44:27.796 --> 00:44:32.147
Elena de Saronelli, he said.

00:44:32.207 --> 00:44:35.437
She had dark eyes and black hair.

00:44:35.497 --> 00:44:37.318
Very beautiful.

00:44:37.379 --> 00:44:40.720
She was half Italian, half Finnish.

00:44:40.781 --> 00:44:43.362
Her brother was a half brother.

00:44:43.422 --> 00:44:48.375
They had the same father, but his mother was Russian, I think.

00:44:48.436 --> 00:44:49.826
Was?

00:44:49.886 --> 00:44:51.418
Had?

00:44:51.478 --> 00:44:54.659
Mr. Harris stared at the guard.

00:44:54.720 --> 00:44:59.553
But she, Elena, she's alive.

00:44:59.613 --> 00:45:01.393
And where is she?

00:45:01.454 --> 00:45:04.324
Oh, no," said the guard.

00:45:04.384 --> 00:45:09.015
Elena de Saronelli died about 80 years ago.

00:45:09.075 --> 00:45:15.518
After she killed her brother with a knife, she jumped off the train and died at once.

00:45:15.578 --> 00:45:18.118
It was near here, I think.

00:45:18.178 --> 00:45:21.109
He looked out of the window into the night.

00:45:21.169 --> 00:45:24.860
Mr. Harris's face was very white again.

00:45:24.920 --> 00:45:27.221
80 years ago?

00:45:27.281 --> 00:45:28.572
He whispered.

00:45:28.632 --> 00:45:30.724
What are you saying?

00:45:30.784 --> 00:45:33.348
Well, she and her brother.

00:45:33.408 --> 00:45:35.558
But I saw them.

00:45:35.618 --> 00:45:39.662
Yes, that's right, the guard said.

00:45:39.722 --> 00:45:43.234
You saw them, but they're not alive.

00:45:43.294 --> 00:45:45.114
They're ghosts.

00:45:45.174 --> 00:45:49.768
They often come on the night train at this time in September.

00:45:49.828 --> 00:45:56.722
I never see them, but somebody saw them last year, a man and his wife.

00:45:56.783 --> 00:45:59.374
They were very unhappy about it.

00:45:59.434 --> 00:46:01.244
But what can I do?

00:46:01.304 --> 00:46:05.905
I can't stop Elena and Carl coming on the train."

00:46:05.965 --> 00:46:09.247
The guard looked at Mr. Harris' white face.

00:46:09.267 --> 00:46:11.589
"'You need a drink?"

00:46:11.649 --> 00:46:12.129
he said.

00:46:12.149 --> 00:46:15.582
"'Come and have a vodka with me."

00:46:15.642 --> 00:46:21.016
Mr. Harris didn't usually drink vodka, but he felt afraid.

00:46:21.076 --> 00:46:28.912
When he closed his eyes, he could see again the laner's long knife and could hear her terrible cry.

00:46:28.973 --> 00:46:33.104
So he went with the guard to the back of the train.

00:46:33.164 --> 00:46:37.387
After the vodka Mr. Harris felt better.

00:46:37.447 --> 00:46:41.719
He didn't want to sleep and the guard was happy to talk.

00:46:41.780 --> 00:46:46.802
So Mr. Harris stayed with the guard and didn't go back to his carriage.

00:46:46.862 --> 00:46:49.828
Yes, the guard said.

00:46:49.888 --> 00:46:52.314
It's a famous story.

00:46:52.374 --> 00:46:54.876
I don't remember it all.

00:46:54.936 --> 00:46:58.668
It happened a long time ago, of course.

00:46:58.728 --> 00:47:04.210
Elena's father was a famous man here in Finland.

00:47:04.270 --> 00:47:11.124
He was very rich once, but he had three or four wives and about eight children.

00:47:11.185 --> 00:47:13.626
And he liked the good things of life.

00:47:13.686 --> 00:47:16.706
So there wasn't much money for the children.

00:47:16.766 --> 00:47:22.318
Carl, the oldest son, was a bad man, people say.

00:47:22.378 --> 00:47:28.002
He wanted an easy life, and money in his hand all the time.

00:47:28.062 --> 00:47:35.606
The train hurried on to Ulu through the Black Knight, and the guard drank some more vodka.

00:47:35.666 --> 00:47:47.210
Now Elena, he said, she didn't have an easy life with those three difficult men, a father, a brother, a husband.

00:47:47.270 --> 00:47:55.855
One year she visited her mother's family in Italy, and there she met her husband, Disaronelli.

00:47:55.915 --> 00:48:00.028
He was rich, but he wasn't a kind man.

00:48:00.089 --> 00:48:04.992
They came back to Finland, and Karl often visited their house.

00:48:05.053 --> 00:48:09.016
He wanted money from his sister's rich husband.

00:48:09.076 --> 00:48:13.454
Elena loved her brother and gave him some money.

00:48:13.514 --> 00:48:19.090
but Desaronelli didn't like Carl and was angry with Elena.

00:48:19.150 --> 00:48:21.731
He stopped giving her money.

00:48:21.791 --> 00:48:27.744
And after that, well, you know the story now.

00:48:27.804 --> 00:48:30.786
Yes, Mr. Harris said.

00:48:30.846 --> 00:48:34.348
Poor, unhappier, Elena.

00:48:34.408 --> 00:48:39.540
Mr. Harris stayed with his friends in Ulou for two weeks.

00:48:39.600 --> 00:48:44.422
They were quiet weeks, and Mr. Harris had a good holiday.

00:48:44.482 --> 00:48:48.112
But he took the bus back to Helsinki.

00:48:48.172 --> 00:48:52.234
The bus was slow, and there were a lot of people on it.

00:48:52.294 --> 00:48:55.196
But Mr. Harris was very happy.

00:48:55.256 --> 00:48:59.238
He didn't want to take the night train across Finland again.

